<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97438" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στῦψις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>contraction, astringency</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Od.</u>
				32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diph.Siph.
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.80f
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.81
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phylotim.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				4.10.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SA</u>
				2.2
			</span></i>; of food which has a <i>costive</i> effect, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Acut.</u>
				10
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aen.Gaz.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				20
			</span></i>; <i>contraction of the skin</i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.216
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in dyeing,
				<i>steeping of the fabric in an astringent solution</i>, to
			prepare it for taking the dye, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Col.</u>
				794a29
			</span></i> (pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in
			perfumery, <i>thickening of oil with certain drugs</i> to make it
			retain the scent longer, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.6
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
